  "summary_en": "Consolidated text of Estonia's Traffic Act, regulating road traffic, vehicle registration, driver licensing and road management. It includes specific provisions on self-driving delivery robots: definitions, a 6 km/h speed limit, use of cycle and pedestrian tracks, give-way duties, and road-owner restrictions.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Defines self-driving delivery robots as partially or fully automated or remotely controlled ground vehicles, with defined users and controllers.",
   "Speed limit of 6 km/h for self-driving delivery robots.",
   "Robots may use pedestrian and cycle tracks and are regulated by pedestrian traffic lights.",
   "Road owners may restrict robot use and must publish restrictions in machine-processable form.",
   "Drivers must give way to delivery robots when turning or leaving the carriageway."
  ],
